{"authored" [{"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3+([\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =3+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/e51b807bc238b140215a8a753fcfe778b14735e723dd5cb43b8aab22039a8e8e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=-2+12=10.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/b8e6f6b7ab2081595723002737bcb73bbced52bfea0f8cfeb91b1201adab0160.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=6.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(6)=-2+9=7\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/C