rification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)={2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=-5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =-5+{\\int }_{1}^{3}({2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5+{[{2}^{2t-2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{2(3)-2}-{2}^{2(1)-2} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{4}-{2}^{0} \\\\  & =-5+16-1 \\\\  & =-5+15 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3+([\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =3+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbf86562e722cc71b8518093bc61a98f3cc08de9a53b2b5016b97cde5a1d986e"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/assets/b8e6f6b7ab2081595723002737bcb73bbced52bfea0f8cfeb91b1201adab0160.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=6.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(6)=-2+9=7\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbf86562e722cc71b8518093bc61a98f3cc08de9a53b2b5016b97cde5a1d986e"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-84264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-84264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =1+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =1+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =1+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =1+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =1+(-0+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-84264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbf86562e722cc71b8518093bc61a98f3cc08de9a53b2b5016b97cde5a1d986e"} {"question" "q-84264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-84264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-84264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/assets/e51b807bc238b140215a8a753fcfe778b14735e723dd5cb43b8aab22039a8e8e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=-2+12=10.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbf86562e722cc71b8518093bc61a98f3cc08de9a53b2b5016b97cde5a1d986e"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)={2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=-5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =-5+{\\int }_{1}^{3}({2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5+{[{2}^{2t-2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{2(3)-2}-{2}^{2(1)-2} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{4}-{2}^{0} \\\\  & =-5+16-1 \\\\  & =-5+15 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbf86562e722cc71b8518093bc61a98f3cc08de9a53b2b5016b97cde5a1d986e"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/state.json" "file_sha256" "792a4954436a81489d436918a9d1c402863e55485a19e380ad7a90cb44e36500"}] "usage" {"q-351463" [] "q-81506" [] "q-81509" [] "q-348321" []} "basis" 2440 "retractions" [[17592186292221 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/b8e6f6b7ab2081595723002737bcb73bbced52bfea0f8cfeb91b1201adab0160.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$"] [17592186292187 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques